  "date": "2026-11-06T10:32:53-06:00",
  "subject": "chore: bump version to v1.0.2096",
  "body": "Signed-off-by: Zach Aller <zach_aller@intuit.com>\n",
  "references": [
    {
      "commit": {
        "author": "\"Zach Aller\" <code@example.com>",
        "date": "2026-10-05T21:32:18-05:00",
        "subject": "fix: clear stale CTP pull request status instead of copying an empty successor status (#2253)",
        "body": "setPullRequestState unconditionally copied the live PullRequest's\nstatus onto ctp.Status.PullRequest, including the window right after\na successor PR is created but before the PullRequest controller has\npopulated its status. That produces an all-empty\nPullRequestCommonStatus, which (every field is omitempty) marshals to\n\"{}\" in the server-side-apply body. Structured-merge turns that into\na JSON null on re-apply (kubernetes/kubernetes#135841), and unlike\nstatus.proposed.dry (+nullable), the CRD schema for status.pullRequest\nrejects a null value, so the full status apply fails and falls back to\na conditions-only apply that leaves the stale pullRequest status in\nplace.\n\nClear ctp.Status.PullRequest to nil in that window instead of copying\nthe empty fields over it. This is safe because\npullRequestUpdateEnqueuesChangeTransferPolicyPredicate already\nre-triggers a CTP reconcile once the new PR's status is populated\n(Status.ID transitions from empty to non-empty), so the real status is\nfilled in on the very next reconcile rather than being lost.\n\nThe existing \"no PR resource found, keep last-known status\" branch\n(len(pr.Items) == 0) is unrelated and unchanged: it is deliberately\nscoped to the PR-object-fully-deleted case (added in #844).\n\nSigned-off-by: Michael Crenshaw <350466+crenshaw-dev@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>",
        "sha": "a183655fbb81f9a639282337b5a2f8f65f81ca31",
        "repoUrl": "https://github.com/argoproj-labs/gitops-promoter"
      }
    }
  ]
}
